# FinTwit Newsletter Agent — Claude Code Build Prompt

## Mission

Build a Python-based financial news monitoring agent that continuously ingests data from X (Twitter), financial news APIs, and macro/earnings calendars — scores each item for market impact — and when a significance threshold is crossed, auto-drafts a concise newsletter via the Claude API and delivers it to the user.

The system should be modular, self-contained, and runnable on a single machine (or a small VPS). Prefer simplicity over scale. SQLite over Postgres. Cron over Kafka.

**Hard constraints:**
- All API calls must be FREE. No paid tiers. If a free option dies, fail gracefully and fall back to the next source.
- X data comes from a curated list of ~15–20 specific accounts, not broad search. This keeps volume low and signal high.
- Primary delivery is Telegram (real-time alerts) + a local web dashboard (monitoring). Email is secondary for daily digests.

