## 3. Unified Data Schema (`ingest/normalizer.py`)

Every data source must be converted to this common schema before storage:

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass, field
from datetime import datetime
from typing import Optional

@dataclass
class NewsItem:
    # Identity
    id: str                          # SHA256 of source + original_id
    source_type: str                 # "x_tweet" | "finnhub" | "polygon" | "newsapi" | "eodhd" | "calendar"
    source_name: str                 # "@DeItaone" | "finnhub_general" | "polygon_news" | etc.
    original_id: str                 # Tweet ID, article ID, etc.

    # Content
    headline: str                    # Tweet text or article title (max 500 chars)
    body: Optional[str] = None       # Article summary/description if available
    url: Optional[str] = None        # Link to original

    # Temporal
    published_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)
    ingested_at: datetime = field(default_factory=datetime.utcnow)

    # Classification (populated by tagger.py)
    tickers: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)     # ["AAPL", "TSLA"]
    topics: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)       # ["fed", "rates", "earnings"]
    category: Optional[str] = None   # "macro" | "earnings" | "geopolitical" | "sector" | "company" | "crypto"

    # Engagement (X-specific, 0 for non-X sources)
    likes: int = 0
    retweets: int = 0
    replies: int = 0
    views: int = 0

    # Scoring (populated by scoring engine)
    urgency_score: float = 0.0       # 0.0 – 1.0, composite score
    velocity_score: float = 0.0      # Sub-score: engagement velocity
    content_score: float = 0.0       # Sub-score: keyword/NLP classification
    market_score: float = 0.0        # Sub-score: price action cross-reference

    # Source metadata
    account_tier: Optional[str] = None   # "wire" | "analysis" | "media"
    credibility: float = 0.5             # From ACCOUNT_RELIABILITY config

    # Dedup
    cluster_id: Optional[str] = None  # Groups duplicate stories
    is_primary: bool = True           # True if this is the "best" version in a cluster
```

